iranian families  forced to flee their country to  different parts of the world including  right here in las vegas victoria saha  spoke to one mother who had just a few  hours to gather her belongings with her  daughters to escape she joins us now in  studio with this exclusive story  ukraine was the only home they ever knew  but life quickly changed forever for so  many ukrainians who had to leave but  escaping ukraine was just the start of  the many hurdles to come  it's my life ludmila inote emstiva shows  us the three small suitcases she had to  pack her life into we just  got in our car we only had six hours to  get ready and we left on february 24th  ludmila and her two daughters said  goodbye to the only home they knew in  venezia  i wasn't sure if my town will be  basically erased and bombed to the  ground she describes the long lines for  the gas station and atm as ukrainians  scrambled to get out we slept in a car  we act in a car four days on the road  led them to the polish border where she  had to say goodbye to her husband of 16  years he had to stay back and fight the  russian army it was ruthless  it's not something that  anybody can survive without getting  traumatized from poland they went to the  netherlands and then to las vegas where  ludmila is staying with her two  daughters thanks to a host family how  are you liking las vegas i  like it really  good as they try to adjust to life in  america there's a constant worry about  the husband and father that was left  behind yeah watching i'm always waking  up and going to sleep with it it's  it never stops that i  don't know when and if i'm going to see  my husband  ludmila and her family visited the  united states a few years ago their  10-year visa allowed them to come here  but it expires in september after which  she'll be applying for a refugee status  she is looking to get a car which would  allow her to hopefully start working her  daughters are 15 and 10 and in need of  summer athletic clothing since all they  were able to bring were their winter  clothes if you would like to donate we  have information up on our website at  8newsnow.com brian victoria
 

